  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The text 'you can be happy and' is mapped onto the prisoners smiling and raising their hands.",
  "description": "The textual phrase 'you can be happy and' is juxtaposed with the visual of prisoners in striped uniforms smiling and raising their hands. This creates an analogical mapping where the text implies that the prisoners are an example of 'you' (the viewer) being happy, despite their grim context. The mapping equates the prisoners' forced or performative happiness with the universal ideal of happiness, ignoring the horrific reality of their situation. This is a harmful mapping that trivializes their suffering and promotes a form of Holocaust minimization.",
